  "answer": "The goal was not met. Four of the five cases were confirmed, each on a different scene (S11, S1, S27, S3), and only three of those are failures the policy caused. In the three policy-caused cases (S11, S1, S27), every run failed in the same way. The other cars were retimed by half a second (0.5 s earlier at S1, 0.5 s later at S11 and S27) at recorded speed. Each time, the policy steered left across the lane line, against a RIGHT command or a recorded path that bore right, and hit a car travelling alongside in the left lane. It did not fail by being hit by a car cutting in. S3 counts as confirmed, but every one of its failures happened before the policy took control: a replayed car (actor 16) drove through the ego during the replay before handoff. So S3 is a flaw in the scenario, not a challenging case for the policy. Each confirmed case rests on only three or four runs, so the ranges show only that their failure rates are above one half, not how much above. No fifth scene was confirmed. Scene 096988dd fails at several delays, but too inconsistently to clear the bar.",
